    {
        "content": "<p>I see that the standard library uses <code>empty : () -&gt; Foo</code> rather than <code>empty : Foo</code>.</p>\n<p>Is there a rationale for that? I tend to use plain constants rather than functions with no args whenever possible, so I'm curious to know why using a function is preferred?</p>",
        "id": 627904159,
        "sender_full_name": "Aurélien Geron",
        "timestamp": 1790715810
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>it's because constants can't be polymorphic</p>",
        "id": 627904788,
        "sender_full_name": "Richard Feldman",
        "timestamp": 1790716008
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>like you can't do <code>x : List(_a)</code></p>",
        "id": 627904878,
        "sender_full_name": "Richard Feldman",
        "timestamp": 1790716025
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>it's a weird edge case we talked about a long time ago <span aria-label=\"sweat smile\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f605\" role=\"img\" title=\"sweat smile\">:sweat_smile:</span></p>",
        "id": 627904923,
        "sender_full_name": "Richard Feldman",
        "timestamp": 1790716039
    },
    {
        "content": "<div class=\"message_inline_image\"><a href=\"https://static.klipy.com/ii/39f2394ae36df6e199be9eb7c9fa1012/7f/99/lusg1qWi.gif\"><img src=\"https://uploads.zulipusercontent.net/92f59ed1d9385d90da56e416212494a8e6207169/68747470733a2f2f7374617469632e6b6c6970792e636f6d2f69692f33396632333934616533366466366531393962653965623763396661313031322f37662f39392f6c757367317157692e676966\"></a></div>",
