        "content": "<p>Thanks <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"281383\">@Richard Feldman</span> .<br>\nIf the function is defined at the top-level and can be evaluated at compile time, then I suppose it will produce the same binary as if I had used a constant instead (of the correct concrete type), right?</p>",
        "id": 627906815,
